Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a small, reliable serverless API with per-tenant isolation, idempotent writes, and TTL in Cosmos DB. It also checks basic validation, simple retries, and test strategy.

Key Concepts

- Azure Functions HTTP trigger and route parameters
- Cosmos DB partitioning by tenantId and idempotent upserts
- JSON payload validation against a minimal schema
- TTL retention in Cosmos DB containers
- Basic retry/backoff and error handling
- Unit and end-to-end testing with local emulation

Code Example

```javascript
// Example outline for the HTTP POST handler
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.params.tenantId;
  const body = req.body;
  // basic validation: eventId required, payload present
  if (!tenantId || !body || !body.eventId) {
    context.res = { status: 400, body: 'Invalid payload' };
    return;
  }
  const item = {
    id: body.eventId,
    tenantId,
    payload: body,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  };
  // upsert to Cosmos DB (idempotent by using eventId as id)
  await cosmosClient.database(DATABASE).container(CONTAINER)
    .items.upsert(item);
  context.res = { status: 200, body: { ok: true } };
};
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this with a local Cosmos DB emulator and simulate retries?
- How would you evolve the schema when new fields are introduced while preserving backward compatibility?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of read-through caching, per-tenant data isolation, and latency optimization in a serverless context. It also surfaces familiarity with common Azure data services and simple failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- Read-through caching with Redis in serverless Functions
- Per-tenant data isolation using Table Storage PartitionKey
- TTL strategy to balance freshness and performance
- Cache stampede mitigation and basic error handling

## Code Example
```csharp
// Minimal illustration for GET endpoint
public async Task<IActionResult> GetCatalog(string tenantId, string productId)
{
    var key = $"{tenantId}:{productId}";
    var cached = await _cache.GetStringAsync(key);
    if (cached != null) return new OkObjectResult(JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Product>(cached));

    var tbl = _table.GetTableReference("Catalog");
    var op = TableOperation.Retrieve<ProductEntity>(tenantId, productId);
    var res = await tbl.ExecuteAsync(op);
    var item = (ProductEntity)res.Result;
    if (item == null) return new NotFoundResult();

    var prod = item.ToProduct();
    await _cache.SetStringAsync(key, JsonConvert.SerializeObject(prod), new DistributedCacheEntryOptions { AbsoluteExpirationRelativeToNow = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(300) });
    return new OkObjectResult(prod);
}
```

